.TH UPGRADE-GUARD 1 "September 2026" "upgrade-guard 0.1.0-beta.1"
.SH NAME
upgrade-guard \- read-only Ubuntu release-upgrade readiness assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B upgrade-guard
scan [--target 26.04] [--format text|json] [--output FILE] [--force]
.br
.B upgrade-guard
export --format json [--output FILE] [--force]
.br
.B upgrade-guard
explain FINDING-ID
.br
.B upgrade-guard
list-checks | version | help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Upgrade Guard inspects read-only system evidence and reports known conditions that can block or complicate an Ubuntu release upgrade.
.PP
Target-release dependency simulation was not performed in this version.
.PP
No system changes were made.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 ready, 1 ready with warnings, 2 blocked, 3 incomplete scan or tool error, 64 command-line usage error.
.SH SAFETY
The program does not install, remove or upgrade packages, run apt update, modify APT sources, change Secure Boot, modify kernels, upload reports or require sudo for ordinary scans.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --target 24.04|26.04
Select the requested target LTS release.
.TP
.B --format text|json
Select stable human-readable or schema-versioned JSON output.
.TP
.B --output FILE
Write the report to a file. Existing files are protected unless
.B --force
is supplied.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable ANSI color.
.TP
.B --verbose
Include passing findings in text output.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/upgrade-guard/schemas/report-v1.schema.json
.br
.I /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/upgrade-guard
